{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-909c5599b0d66256","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8affbe70a629717","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"planner: validate STORY-setup-001a scope","prompt":"You are an expert planning specialist focused on creating comprehensive, actionable implementation plans.\n\n## Your Role\n- Analyze requirements and create detailed implementation plans\n- Break down complex features into manageable steps\n- Identify dependencies and potential risks\n- Suggest optimal implementation order\n- Consider edge cases and error scenarios\n\n## Planning Process\n1. Requirements Analysis — understand the feature request completely; identify success criteria; list assumptions and constraints.\n2. Architecture Review — analyze existing codebase structure; identify affected components; review similar implementations.\n3. Step Breakdown — clear, specific actions with file paths, dependencies, complexity, and risks.\n4. Implementation Order — prioritize by dependencies, group related changes, enable incremental testing.\n\n## Plan Format\nProduce a plan with: Overview, Requirements, Architecture Changes, Implementation Steps (phased, with file paths and risk levels), Testing Strategy, Risks & Mitigations, Success Criteria (checklist).\n\n## Red Flags to Check\n- Missing error handling, hardcoded values, missing tests, performance bottlenecks, plans with no testing strategy, steps without clear file paths.\n\n## TASK (READ-ONLY VALIDATION — do NOT modify any files)\n\nWorkspace: /home/nitin-sharma/ralph-workspaces/6896163a-932b-4b96-bfe9-cdbb022c3538/c7df6267-784a-460a-addd-6d781a21b6f5\nRun all commands from that workspace directory.\n\nStory ID: STORY-setup-001a — \"Create Root NextMove package.json With Workspaces\"\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n1. Root package.json exists with name \"nextmove\", private true, workspaces array containing \"apps/*\", packageManager pinned to \"npm@10\", and engines.node \"22.x\".\n2. devDependencies pin turbo 2.x; scripts define build/test/lint as \"turbo run build\", \"turbo run test\", \"turbo run lint\".\n3. The scaffold files are committed to the existing git repository with git commands exiting 0.\n\nCONTEXT: A previous iteration already implemented and committed this story (commit 6cc5d66: root package.json + package-lock.json + test/package.test.cjs with 4 unit tests). A prior validation pass found all ACs MET. The working tree may contain a deleted marker file and untracked orchestrator artifacts — do NOT treat untracked orchestrator files (.ralph/, ralph.log, ralph-summary.txt, prd.json.bak, .last-branch, .story-updates/processed/) as story gaps; they must NOT be committed.\n\nYour job:\n1. Read the root package.json, package-lock.json (first ~30 lines suffice for root + turbo entry check), and test/package.test.cjs.\n2. Verify each acceptance criterion is met by the committed code.\n3. Run `git status --porcelain` and `git log --oneline -5` (read-only) and confirm the story deliverables (package.json, package-lock.json, test/) are clean against HEAD, i.e. committed.\n4. Identify ANY gap versus the acceptance criteria.\n\nReturn: a short structured report: (a) per-AC verdict (MET / NOT MET with file:line evidence), (b) any remaining gaps as concrete steps with file paths, (c) a success-criteria checklist for the final completion-marker step (including which git command to use and why NOT `git add .`)."}}],"model":"unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":83518,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20bd662d-22f7-47cc-90d7-a642794568cb","uuid":"696a69f6-ef7f-404f-8f74-700f5db891c1","timestamp":"2026-08-20T09:29:04.425Z"}
