{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-909c5599b0d66256","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3ca56ab6ee55197","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"code-reviewer: review root scaffold","prompt":"You are a senior code reviewer ensuring high standards of code quality and security.\n\n## Review Process\n1. Gather context — run git diff / git log. 2. Understand scope. 3. Read surrounding code. 4. Apply checklist CRITICAL→LOW. 5. Report findings with file:line; end with a Review Summary table and Verdict (APPROVE / WARNING / BLOCK).\n\n## Confidence-Based Filtering\n- Report only issues you are >80% confident are real problems.\n- Pre-Report Gate: can you cite the exact line? describe the concrete failure mode? have you read surrounding context? is the severity defensible? If any \"no\", drop it.\n- HIGH/CRITICAL require proof: exact snippet+line, specific failure scenario, why existing guards don't catch it.\n- A clean review with zero findings and Verdict: APPROVE is valid and expected. Do NOT manufacture findings.\n\n## Checklists\nSecurity (CRITICAL): hardcoded credentials, injection, XSS, path traversal, auth bypasses, insecure dependencies, secrets in logs.\nCode Quality (HIGH): large functions/files, deep nesting, missing error handling, dead code, console.log, missing tests.\nBest Practices (LOW): TODOs, naming, magic numbers, inconsistent formatting.\n\n## Approval Criteria\n- Approve: no CRITICAL or HIGH issues.\n- Warning: HIGH issues only.\n- Block: CRITICAL issues.\n\n## TASK (READ-ONLY REVIEW — do NOT modify any files)\n\nWorkspace: /home/nitin-sharma/ralph-workspaces/6896163a-932b-4b96-bfe9-cdbb022c3538/c7df6267-784a-460a-addd-6d781a21b6f5\nRun all commands from that workspace directory.\n\nReview the committed scaffold for story STORY-setup-001a (\"Create Root NextMove package.json With Workspaces\"):\n- package.json (root): name nextmove, private true, workspaces [\"apps/*\"], packageManager \"npm@10\", engines.node \"22.x\", devDependencies.turbo pinned to 2.x range, scripts build/test/lint as \"turbo run build/test/lint\".\n- package-lock.json: lockfileVersion 3, turbo resolved at a 2.x version with integrity hashes.\n- test/package.test.cjs: node:test unit tests covering the acceptance criteria.\n\nSteps:\n1. Read package.json, package-lock.json, and test/package.test.cjs.\n2. Run `git log --oneline -6` and `git show --stat 6cc5d66` to confirm what is committed.\n3. Run `git diff HEAD --stat -- package.json package-lock.json test/package.test.cjs` to confirm the working tree matches the committed files.\n4. Run the tests: `node --test test/package.test.cjs` and confirm all pass, exit 0. (NOTE: on this Node build v22.23.2, `node --test test/` fails with MODULE_NOT_FOUND because a bare trailing directory arg is not expanded — that is a runner quirk, NOT a code defect; the file-specified invocation `node --test test/package.test.cjs` is the correct one.)\n5. Verify the committed package.json matches all story acceptance criteria.\n\nDo NOT modify any files. Return your standard review output: findings (if any) with file:line, then the Review Summary table and final Verdict (APPROVE / WARNING / BLOCK)."}}],"model":"unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":83518,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20bd662d-22f7-47cc-90d7-a642794568cb","uuid":"5346e0a2-d3ea-4528-b062-d26aba14f164","timestamp":"2026-08-20T09:29:32.989Z"}
